{# THE CREATE SCREEN — an area from its identity, and a boundary that is optional.

   Design: areas/new.html in the design workspace.

   IDENTITY FIRST, BOUNDARY OPTIONAL. The create flow no longer makes the
   boundary import BE the creation. An area is born from a name (IUCN category
   and the established year are the gazetted facts, both optional), and the
   boundary is a choice on the same screen: add it now — the file is imported as
   the area is created — or add it later, which creates the area at once and
   lands it on its overview's no-boundary state, where the same
   BoundaryImportService waits inline. AreaCreator makes the area;
   BoundaryImport puts the edge on it.

   NO LIVE IMPORT PIPELINE, and that is an architectural deviation rather than an
   unfinished one — see the note carried on this screen before: the steps the
   design's pipeline card narrates all belong to the GDAL conversion path this
   module does not have, and what is left (parse one GeoJSON document, insert one
   row) finishes in milliseconds and has nothing to watch.

   THE FORMAT LIST IS THE ONE THIS MODULE CAN ACTUALLY READ — GeoJSON, because
   the four other formats need GDAL on the host.

   THE PLATE CARRIES NO WIDGET INDEX — the design file's `PL·` labels are the
   workspace's referencing system and not product. See
   tests/Unit/Template/NoWorkshopLabelsTest.php. #}
{% extends '@Shell/page.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}New area{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {{ include('@Area/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}

{# Not inside an area yet — there is nothing for the tab strip to be about. #}
{% block shell_page_tabs %}{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}<a href="{{ path('area_index') }}">uhifadhi</a> / <a href="{{ path('area_index') }}">areas</a> / new area{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}New area{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}An area starts as a name. Its boundary is optional &mdash; add it now, or create the area and add it later from its overview.{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_actions %}
    <a class="tgl" href="{{ path('area_index') }}">&larr; Back to areas</a>
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page %}
    {# The area is created from its identity; the boundary is optional. Both cards
       live in ONE form, so a single "Create area" finishes the job whichever
       boundary choice is made. Mirrors the edit-area identity + boundary layout. #}
    <form class="grid g32" style="align-items:start" method="post" action="{{ path('area_new') }}"
          enctype="multipart/form-data" data-controller="uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload">

        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ token }}">

        {# IDENTITY — an area is a name first. IUCN and the established year are
           the gazetted facts; both optional, because an area drawn by hand has
           neither. #}
        <div class="c" id="identity">
            <span class="tab">Identity<span class="src">&middot; area_of_interest</span></span>

            <div class="ed-cardhd">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z"/><path d="M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z"/></svg>
                <span>An area starts as a name. The boundary is optional and never blocks creation &mdash; <b>add it now, or add it later</b>. IUCN category and the established year are the gazetted facts, and an area drawn by hand has neither.</span>
            </div>

            {% if error %}
                {# THE REFUSAL SITS ON THE FORM IT CAME FROM, and every typed
                   field is still in place: whoever was refused only has to fix
                   the one thing the sentence names. #}
                <p class="import-error" role="alert">{{ error }}</p>
            {% endif %}

            <label class="fldlab" for="area-name">Name <span class="opt">required</span></label>
            <input class="fld" id="area-name" name="name" value="{{ name }}" required
                   placeholder="Area name &mdash; as its official record names it"
                   aria-label="Area name" style="margin-bottom:14px">

            <div class="grid g2" style="gap:14px;margin-bottom:0">
                <div>
                    <label class="fldlab" for="area-iucn">IUCN category <span class="opt">optional</span></label>
                    <select class="fld" id="area-iucn" name="iucn" aria-label="IUCN category">
                        <option value=""{{ iucn is empty ? ' selected' : '' }}>Not assigned</option>
                        {% for cat in ['Ia', 'Ib', 'II', 'III', 'IV', 'V', 'VI'] %}
                            <option{{ iucn == cat ? ' selected' : '' }}>{{ cat }}</option>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </select>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <label class="fldlab" for="area-established">Established <span class="opt">optional</span></label>
                    <input class="fld" id="area-established" name="established" value="{{ established }}"
                           placeholder="Year" inputmode="numeric" aria-label="Established year">
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="use">Plain metadata, saved with the area. The boundary and its derived size are added by the import &mdash; never typed here.</div>
        </div>

        {# BOUNDARY — the optional half. "Now" imports the file as the area is
           created; "later" creates it bare and lands it on the overview's
           no-boundary state, where the inline import CTA and Edit area both reuse
           this same import on the existing area. #}
        <div class="c card-bound" id="boundary">
            <span class="tab">Boundary<span class="src">&middot; optional</span></span>

            <div class="bchoice">
                <label class="bopt">
                    <input type="radio" name="boundary_mode" value="now"{{ boundary_mode != 'later' ? ' checked' : '' }}>
                    <span class="bdot"></span>
                    <span class="btxt"><b>Add the boundary now</b><em>Upload the gazetted boundary and it is imported as the area is created.</em></span>
                </label>
                <label class="bopt">
                    <input type="radio" name="boundary_mode" value="later"{{ boundary_mode == 'later' ? ' checked' : '' }}>
                    <span class="bdot"></span>
                    <span class="btxt"><b>Add it later</b><em>Create the area with no boundary. You land on its overview with an inline import prompt, and can add one any time from Edit area.</em></span>
                </label>
            </div>

            <div class="drop-wrap">
                <label class="drop" data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload-target="drop"
                       data-action="dragover->uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload#over dragleave->uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload#leave drop->uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload#drop">
                    <input type="file" name="boundary" accept=".geojson,.json,application/geo+json,application/json"
                           data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload-target="file" data-action="uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload#chosen" aria-label="Boundary file">
                    <span data-uhifadhi--area-bundle--area-upload-target="label">Drop your boundary here &mdash; or click to choose</span>
                    <span class="mono">GeoJSON &mdash; a Polygon, a MultiPolygon, a Feature or a FeatureCollection; several features are merged into one boundary</span>
                </label>
                <div class="mono drop-note">Coordinates are taken as they arrive: GeoJSON is WGS84 by definition, so nothing is reprojected. The geometry is checked by PostGIS at the moment of the insert.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="form-foot">
                <a class="tgl" href="{{ path('area_index') }}">Cancel</a>
                <button type="submit" class="cta">Create area</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </form>
{% endblock %}
